# Component Design Standards

## Structure

- Functional components only, as arrow functions with a default export:

```tsx
const FeatureCard = ({ title }: FeatureCardProps) => {
  return <div>{title}</div>;
};

export default FeatureCard;
```

- Add `'use client';` as the first line **only** when the component uses hooks, state, browser APIs, or event handlers. Keep components server components by default.
- One component per file. When a section grows, split presentational pieces into sibling files (e.g. `featureCard.tsx`, `icons.tsx`) and compose them from the section `index.tsx`.

## DRY & Composition

- Reuse shared primitives instead of re-implementing them (e.g. always use `@/components/ui/button`, never hand-roll a styled link button).
- Render repeated UI by mapping over a local data array (see `pricingOptions`, `faqItems`, `countries`) rather than copy-pasting markup.
- Extract a sub-component once markup repeats or a block exceeds ~40 lines / has its own concern.

## Separation of Concerns

- Data arrays and config live at the top of the component; markup stays declarative below.
- Keep layout/routing in pages and modules; keep visual rendering in components. Don't fetch or compute business logic inside presentational components.

## TypeScript Typing

- Type every prop. Use a `PascalCase` `...Props` interface for reusable/multi-prop components; inline object types are acceptable for tiny local components.
- Type state and refs explicitly when not obvious (`useState<number | null>(0)`, `useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null)`).
- Never use `any`. Use library types (`StaticImageData`, `Swiper as SwiperType`).

## Accessibility (required on every component)

- Icon-only buttons/links need `aria-label`; logo links include an `sr-only` text label.
- Interactive accordions/toggles set state-reflecting attributes (`aria-expanded`).
- All `Image`/`img` need meaningful `alt`; external links use `target="_blank"` with `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Use semantic elements: `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<footer>`, headings in order.

## Avoid Anti-Patterns

- No prop drilling more than ~2 levels — compose or colocate instead.
- No unnecessary state or effects; derive values during render when possible.
- No inline narrating comments. Add a comment only to explain non-obvious intent or a constraint (see the marquee animation math).
